# Copy to .env.local and fill in.
#
# Create an API token at: https://id.atlassian.com/manage-profile/security/api-tokens
# The token needs only read access to the DDT Jira projects.

JIRA_BASE_URL=https://onetakeda.atlassian.net
JIRA_EMAIL=you@takeda.com
JIRA_API_TOKEN=

# Optional: override the "today" used for risk derivation, for reproducible runs.
# Format: YYYY-MM-DD
# SNAPSHOT_AS_OF=2026-08-05


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OData feed probe (npm run probe-odata). Read-only; answers E1-E3, E5 and E7
# in reference/adr-001-data-source.md. NOT used by the sync.
#
# The feed is the Alpha Serve Power BI Connector export endpoint that powers the
# DDTRoadmap Power BI solution. Probed 2026-08-06: reachable from an ordinary
# workstation (no on-prem gateway), and it answers 401 with
# "WWW-Authenticate: Basic". The URL token alone grants nothing.
#
# Treat the feed URL as a secret: keep it in .env.local, never commit it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ODATA_FEED_URL=https://powerbi-cloud-prod.alphaservesp.com/api/export/power-bi/<token>
# ODATA_AUTH_MODE=basic                  # basic | bearer | oauth2 | anonymous

# basic -- the scheme this endpoint actually advertises.
# Ask for a SERVICE credential, not a personal login: a named individual's
# account relocates the key-person dependency the OData move exists to remove,
# and ties the roadmap's data scope to that person's Jira permissions.
#
# ODATA_USERNAME MUST BE THE EMAIL OF THE ACCOUNT THAT OWNS THIS EXPORT TOKEN.
# The endpoint validates the pair, and a mismatch answers `401 Email mismatch`
# rather than a generic failure. So swapping ODATA_FEED_URL to a different feed
# usually means swapping ODATA_USERNAME too -- otherwise it reads as a bad
# credential when it is actually an ownership mismatch. For reference, the other
# 401 bodies are `Empty Authorization header` (nothing sent) and
# `Email is invalid` (username blank or malformed).
# ODATA_USERNAME=
# ODATA_PASSWORD=

# Retained for other feeds; not advertised by this endpoint.
# ODATA_TOKEN=
# ODATA_TOKEN_URL=
# ODATA_CLIENT_ID=
# ODATA_CLIENT_SECRET=
# ODATA_SCOPE=

# Only needed if auto-detection of the payload shape fails.
# ODATA_ISSUE_ENTITY=
# ODATA_PROJECT_KEY_FIELD=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Serving the app from the OData feed (WP5).
#
# The same ODATA_* variables above are used; nothing additional is required to
# read the feed. Entity-set names are discovered from the service document, so
# there is no list to configure.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Which source the application serves. Default: snapshot.
#
# `odata` is an explicit OPT-IN and is never inferred from a credential being
# present. Flipping the default is migration step 6 and needs governance
# sign-off (E4/E6/E8 in reference/adr-001-data-source.md are still open).
# ROADMAP_SOURCE=odata

# States which of the three Alpha Serve sources ODATA_FEED_URL points at.
# They share one host and differ only by token, so the URL cannot tell them
# apart. Used in provenance; the shape guard checks the claim against what the
# service actually serves. Default: "Feed #3".
# ODATA_FEED_LABEL=Feed #3

# How long one read is served before the feed is re-read. Default: 900 (15 min).
# This bounds both data staleness and `asOf` drift, so a long-lived server
# cannot keep evaluating risk against yesterday's date. 0 reads every time.
# ODATA_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS=900


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Issue type hierarchy capture (npm run capture-issue-types).
#
# Uses JIRA_BASE_URL / JIRA_EMAIL / JIRA_API_TOKEN above. Jira REST is the ONLY
# source of `issuetype.hierarchyLevel` -- no OData feed exposes it -- and
# `classifyIssues` selects roadmap items by it. Run this to populate
# ISSUE_TYPE_LEVELS in config/feed.ts before serving from the feed; an
# unregistered type is a blocking diagnostic by design, because the
# alternative is silently dropping a site's work.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
